<title>BELGIUM: EU clears research aid to Usinor Sacilor.</title>
<headline>EU clears research aid to Usinor Sacilor.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had aproved a French research grant for a project carried by steel makers Usinor Sacilor SA of France and Thyssen AG of Germany.</p>
<p>It said the project, relating to the continuous thin-strip casting process, cost a total 96 million francs over three years and would be financed evenly by the two partners.</p>
<p>Usinor Sacilor would, however, receive 12 million francs from the French state, which the Commission cleared on the grounds that Europe must not be left behind in a field where international competitors are more advanced.</p>
<p>The Commission also aproved another French aid of 17.5 million francs to help Usinor Sacilor adapt steel-making processes to use scrap.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
